# Change a claim's status (open, settle, approve, reject, void, resettle, delete or restore). A DRAFT claim is deleted (DELETED, counted nowhere) and restored to a DRAFT only on the sheet-today it was deleted. A clerk's settle above the clerk limit leaves it PENDING for a steward to approve or reject. A steward's resettle freezes a SETTLED claim again at today's figure; a steward may void a SETTLED claim within 7 days of its settlement, its frozen figure leaving every total. A refused change (not allowed from the claim's status or by this user, unknown claim, a claim dated in a closed period, an open past its period's cap on the person's OPEN or PENDING claims, a void without a reason from the sheet's list while it has any) writes nothing, not even an audit line.
